Modifications: every one of the 587 unique trips and 110 stages is kept.
The fields are renamed; the vehicle is named from the agency code (taxi:
"Minibus taxi", the codebook's 14-seater; bus: "Bus"); the two-letter
district codes are named Kampala (KA), Wakiso (WA) and Mukono (MU). The
codebook reads MU as Mpigi, but the three stages coded MU are Mukono Taxi
Park, Seeta Stage and Misindye Ssonde, in Mukono District, so the
template names it Mukono. A fare of 0 is read as no fare recorded (51
trips). Lengths are rounded to 10 m and positions to five decimal places,
about a metre. The study draws each stage as an outline; the template
marks it with a point inside that outline. The map's SQL works out each
trip's fare per kilometre and its band.


